I. PREFACE: THE ARCHITECTURAL SINGULARITY
Traditional digital interconnects, governed by static bus widths and buffered Multi-Link Aggregation (MLA), have reached a physical impasse. As lane counts (N) increase in standards like PCIe Gen 7+ or CXL, the "Coordination Tax"—manifesting as clock skew, buffer bloat, and iterative Forward Error Correction (FEC) latency—grows exponentially. This creates non-deterministic jitter and thermal instability.

PHX-BusLink, conceived by Juho Artturi Hemminki, is the definitive departure from static bus logic. It is a dynamic, self-morphing orchestration layer that manages the connective fabric between lanes. PHX-BusLink enables a seamless transition from a single lane to an infinite array (N -> infinity) while maintaining a fixed, single-cycle (Deterministic) latency profile. It is the first protocol to treat parallel data as a coherent mathematical field rather than discrete packets.

II. THE DYNAMIC MORPHING PROTOCOL
The PHX-BusLink does not operate on a fixed logic set; it adapts its operational mode based on the density and electromagnetic environment of the interconnect array.

Phase 1: Direct-Sync Mode (N < 1,024)
At low densities, PHX-BusLink functions as an ultra-low latency point-to-point interface. The G-STORM core manages individual lane alignment using a 9-bit Delta Update mechanism that neutralizes physical trace length variances in real-time.

Phase 2: Coherent-Mesh Mode (N = 10^3 to 10^12)
As the array scales into the billions of lanes, PHX-BusLink shifts into a "Swarm Intelligence" state. It ceases to fight electromagnetic crosstalk and instead harvests it. Inductive energy between adjacent lanes is utilized as a secondary carrier, reinforcing the primary signal and reducing the power required for transmission.

Phase 3: Universal Continuum Mode (N -> infinity)
At the limit of infinity, the PHX-BusLink achieves mathematical saturation. The boundaries between individual physical lanes vanish. Information is transmitted as a continuous wave-front that is present across the entire fabric simultaneously. In this state, the link becomes functionally indestructible; the loss of a billion lanes is mathematically irrelevant to the integrity of the stream.

